1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,867
Every site you learn from starts from zero.

2
00:00:03,867 --> 00:00:07,333
Nema fixes that. I want to show you three ways I use it.

3
00:00:15,073 --> 00:00:23,733
A cooking course I have never opened. It wants to know three things about me. It asks my nema, not me.

4
00:00:24,073 --> 00:00:26,593
I say yes. That is all it gets.

5
00:00:28,173 --> 00:00:32,993
68 minutes become 27. It skips what I already know.

6
00:00:35,883 --> 00:00:40,433
Every page shows what it can do with WebMCP.

7
00:00:44,173 --> 00:00:52,823
I do one exercise. The course gives me a note that says I passed. That note is mine. I keep it in my nema.

8
00:00:59,733 --> 00:01:02,217
Now a different site. It has never seen the first one.

9
00:01:02,217 --> 00:01:04,700
But it already knows.

10
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:11,180
A different site. It asks, I say yes, and it already counts what I did before.

11
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:17,310
Two lessons are already done. The page names the prerequisite I still need.

12
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:22,910
With the extension it is one click. My notes come home alone.

13
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:31,240
This is a real article, with questions inside the text.

14
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:34,217
And which AI is this?

15
00:01:34,217 --> 00:01:35,633
The one you already use.

16
00:01:36,583 --> 00:01:41,233
Any agent can use it, and my nema answers only what I approve.

17
00:01:43,383 --> 00:01:46,283
One manifest block and one script tag. That is all.

18
00:01:46,753 --> 00:01:50,353
If you teach on the web, you can add this in one minute.

19
00:01:51,033 --> 00:01:54,133
What you learn is yours. Not the sites'. So, that is nema.

20
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:57,233
Please try it. We would love your feedback.

